{"availability":"available","full":"LeNPaul/portfolio-jekyll-theme","name":"portfolio-jekyll-theme","description":"A minimalist Jekyll theme for building a personal portfolio site powered by Jekyll and GitHub Pages","category":"Design","language":"SCSS","stars":249,"forks":505,"created":"2016-09-05T21:02:25Z","updated":"2024-05-13T16:45:17Z","license":"MIT","branch":"gh-pages","homepage":"https://lenpaul.github.io/portfolio-jekyll-theme/","topics":["blog","github-pages","jekyll","jekyll-blog","jekyll-site","jekyll-template","jekyll-theme","minimalist","portfolio","theme"],"demo":"https://lenpaul.github.io/portfolio-jekyll-theme/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T19:01:16.769Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T19:01:16.769Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T19:01:16.769Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T07:21:54.265Z","stars":249,"forks":503},{"at":"2026-10-08T09:23:57.374Z","stars":249,"forks":505},{"at":"2026-10-10T19:01:16.769Z","stars":249,"forks":505}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a Jekyll theme built using the DevTips Starter Kit as a foundation for starting, and following closely the amazing tutorial by Travis Neilson over at DevTips. The purpose of this theme is to provide a clean and simple website for your portfolio. Emphasis is placed on your projects, which are shown front and center on the home page.","Everything that you will ever need to know about this Jekyll theme is included in the README below, which you can also find in the demo site. For a guide on how to deploy a Jekyll site using GitHub Pages, please check out this article.","If you like my work then please consider supporting me with Ko-fi."],"features":["Portfolio Jekyll Theme was designed to be a minimalist theme in order for the focus to remain on your content. For example, links are signified mainly through coloured font, in order to maximize the perceived affordance…","Portfolio Jekyll Theme supports comments at the end of posts through Disqus. In order to activate Disqus commenting, set disqus.comments to true in the data/settings.yml file. If you do not have a Disqus account…","It is possible to track your site statistics through Google Analytics. Similar to Disqus, you will have to create an account for Google Analytics, and enter the correct Google ID for your site under google-ID in the…","Atom is supported by default through jekyll-feed. With jekyll-feed, you can set configuration variables such as 'title', 'description', and 'author', in the config.yml file.","All social media icons are courtesy of Font Awesome. You can change which icons appear, as well as the account that they link to, in the settings.yml file in the data folder."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LeNPaul/portfolio-jekyll-theme/blob/gh-pages/README.md","fingerprint":"0c67c943ec20fe88613d8a02e2bf7676c25df51499ff986b25c922f351907f77","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T07:21:54.458Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T07:21:54.458Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This is a Jekyll theme built using the DevTips Starter Kit as a foundation for starting, and following closely the amazing tutorial by Travis Neilson over at DevTips. The purpose of this theme is to provide a clean and simple website for your portfolio. Emphasis is placed on your projects, which are shown front and center on the home page.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LeNPaul/portfolio-jekyll-theme/blob/gh-pages/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Similar to Disqus, you will have to create an account for Google Analytics, and enter the correct Google ID for your site under google-ID in the settings.yml file.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LeNPaul/portfolio-jekyll-theme/blob/gh-pages/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"0c67c943ec20fe88613d8a02e2bf7676c25df51499ff986b25c922f351907f77","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LeNPaul/portfolio-jekyll-theme/blob/gh-pages/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-